  "final_message": "I built the notes app on the existing project. In local tests the API calls behaved as specified, the frontend typechecks and builds, and a local gunicorn server served `/api/health`, the frontend, and a 401 for an anonymous write. I couldn't build the Docker image because Docker isn't available here, and I didn't click through the frontend in a browser.\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`)\n- All the endpoints you listed are in place. Data is stored in SQLite at `./data/app.db`, which is created on startup.\n- Passwords are stored hashed, and so are login tokens.\n- Rejected input returns 400 with `{\"error\": ..., \"errors\": {field: message}}`. The frontend shows these messages next to the matching form fields.\n- A non-author trying to change or delete a note gets 403; a missing note gets 404. A taken username at registration gets 409.\n- `updated_at` always moves forward on an update, even if two updates land in the same microsecond.\n- `q` searches titles, content and tags, ignoring case. `page_size` is capped at 100.\n\n**Things I added beyond the spec**\n- Three extra endpoints: `GET /api/auth/me` and `POST /api/auth/logout` (used by the frontend), and a catch-all that returns a JSON 404 for unknown `/api` paths.\n- Registration also returns a token, so new users are signed in straight away.\n- I set limits you didn't specify:\n  - usernames: 3\u201364 characters, letters, digits, `_ . @ -`\n  - passwords: at least 6 characters\n  - titles: required, up to 200 characters\n  - tags: no commas, up to 50 characters each, up to 20 per note\n\n**One behaviour to decide on:** tags keep the case they were typed in, so `Work` and `work` count as two separate tags. Should they be treated as the same tag instead?\n\n**Frontend** (React + TypeScript + Tailwind)\n- Registration and sign-in forms, with the signed-in username and a sign-out button in the header.\n- Note list with pinned notes highlighted, a search box, an author filter, paging, and a tag cloud that filters the list.\n- Note page that shows content as plain text with line breaks kept.\n- Create and edit forms with a tag input that suggests existing tags.\n- On your own notes: edit, pin/unpin, and delete with a confirmation.\n\n**Other changes**\n- `npm run build` now runs a TypeScript check before building, and there's a separate `npm run typecheck`.\n- I added `frontend/tsconfig.json`, a `.gitignore`, and new frontend dependencies, with `package-lock.json` updated to match.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
